            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral functioning Vineberg grafts. A 25-year follow-up.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>824-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a 25-year follow-up of angiographically proven bilateral functioning Vineberg grafts. This represents the longest angiographic follow-up found in the literature. The relevance of these grafts in present-day revascularization procedures is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
